      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>These are good, thanks. They feel pretty authentic. \n\nActually, looking at the backend results for these, the positivity score is coming in a bit lower than I expected for a \"Luxury\" tier test. It's only hitting maybe a 0.7 out of 1.0. I need to see if the dashboard can handle higher intensity values, so I need a second batch of 5 reviews.\n\nTry to make these a bit more enthusiastic—like, really glowing. But again, I'm stressing: please don't just spam a list of adjectives. I need them to still feel like real customers talking about specific things (the spa, the pool, the staff, etc.), even if they're being extra positive. Just try to get that score up a nudge without making them look like bots.",
